=== P3/A5/0001 — Android data layer + ViewModels ===
Artifact: apps/android/** — KMP shared StateFlow state holders bound to lifecycle-aware Compose ViewModels (ADR-013 cache-then-network).
Severity: Data foundation (blocks all Android A7 page prompts). Delegation: FORBIDDEN (done in-session).

=== STEP 1 — SURVEY: shared-core state holders / web hook groups -> Android ViewModel mapping by domain ===

Shared-core S8 state holders surveyed (apps/shared/core/.../presentation/**): every domain exposes
hot StateFlow<Resource<T>> feeds (cache-then-network, ADR-013) + non-throwing suspend Result<> mutations,
mirroring the web TanStack hook domains (web/src/api/hooks/**). Resource<T> = Loading(cached,fetchedAt,stale)
| Success(data,fetchedAt) | Error(cached,fetchedAt,stale,error). Repos: Http*Repository(api, store, clock).

Android binding layer (this artifact) maps shared holders -> Compose UI state. It adds NO networking /
business logic (ADR-002); it consumes the shared holders and re-shares them lifecycle-aware.

  Web hook group              Shared S8 holder         Android ViewModel binding (A5 foundation / A7 widens)
  --------------------------  -----------------------  -----------------------------------------------------
  useDashboard                DashboardStore           DashboardViewModel  (single read + refresh)            [built]
  useVehicles                 VehiclesStore            VehiclesListViewModel (list + sync mutation + select)  [built]
  useVehicle/useVehicleState  VehiclesStore            VehicleDetailViewModel (detail+state, wake command)    [built]
  useSettings (+ useUnits)    SettingsStore            DataContainer.unitFormatter (SI->display boundary)     [built]
  (selected vehicle context)  —                        SelectedVehicleStore (app-scoped, self-healing)        [built]
  useCharging/useDriving/
  useEnergy/useAnalytics/
  useTelemetry/useTrips/
  useNotifications/useAdmin/
  useExports/useLocations/
  useUser/useVehicleSystems   <existing shared stores> A7 page ViewModels (extend DataContainer + factory)   [A7 widens]

Common base patterns/utilities provided for every page ViewModel (data/**):
  - UiState<T> + UiPhase + ErrorKind         : the lifecycle-aware Compose projection of Resource<T>;
                                               loading/cached/refreshing/empty/stale/error/retry in one type.
  - ResourceUiState.toUiState()/errorKindOf  : the single pure Resource->UiState mapper (off-device testable).
  - BaseFeedViewModel                        : viewModelScope re-sharing (StateFlow & Flow .asUiState() with
                                               WhileSubscribed), one-shot UiEvent channel, redacting logger.
  - SelectedVehicleStore                     : app-scoped selected vehicle; reconcile() self-heals from list.
  - PaginationState / Filtering(Sort/DateRange/FilterState) : pure list-control utilities.
  - CommandRunner / CommandState             : confirm-then-run command state machine (ADR-013: never cache
                                               write-intent as applied; only the real backend Result advances).
  - UnitFormatter / UnitPreferences          : SI display boundary; fromSettings() ports web useUnits derivation.
  - DataContainer + LocalDataContainer + dataViewModel() : DI graph + ViewModelProvider.Factory + Compose entry.

Lifecycle collection pattern (A7 pages): val vm: XViewModel = dataViewModel(); val s by vm.state.collectAsStateWithLifecycle().

Deliverables (apps/android):
  data/UiState.kt, ResourceUiState.kt, UiEvent.kt, BaseFeedViewModel.kt
  data/PaginationState.kt, Filtering.kt, SelectedVehicleStore.kt, CommandRunner.kt, UnitFormatter.kt
  data/DataContainer.kt, LocalDataContainer.kt
  data/dashboard/DashboardViewModel.kt, data/vehicles/VehiclesListViewModel.kt, data/vehicles/VehicleDetailViewModel.kt
  edits: auth/AuthContainer.kt (owns DataContainer + diagnostics; clears selection on sign-out), ui/App.kt
         (provides LocalDataContainer), build.gradle.kts + gradle/libs.versions.toml (lifecycle-viewmodel/
         runtime-compose + kotlinx-serialization-json, pinned to shared-core versions).
  tests (src/test/.../data): ResourceUiState, Pagination, Filtering, SelectedVehicle, CommandRunner,
         UnitFormatter, RedactedLogging, dashboard/DashboardViewModel, vehicles/{VehiclesList,VehicleDetail}
         (fake shared StateFlows via fake repositories over the REAL shared stores).

